Subject: [PATCH] Do not probe for pipe2

The iOS 27 SDK declares pipe2 for the first time, marked as introduced in
iOS 27. Anything targeting an earlier iOS gets a weak import, so the call
in g_unix_open_pipe lands on NULL -- and gwakeup.c reaches it for every
GWakeup, because Darwin has no eventfd. That is a crash on every device
below iOS 27.

Removing the probe cannot be done in CFLAGS: meson's has_function writes
its own `char pipe2 (void);` declaration rather than using the header, so
the availability attribute never reaches the compiler and the probe says
yes however hard -Wunguarded-availability-new is turned up. Dropping the
name from the list is the only place the answer can be changed.

The fallback right below it is plain pipe() plus an fcntl for FD_CLOEXEC,
non-atomic but perfectly correct, and it is what this build used until the
SDK bump.

pipe2 is the only entry in this list the iOS 27 SDK puts beyond our 18.0
deployment target; the rest are either older than that or absent from the
SDK entirely, so meson's answer for them is already the right one.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -720,7 +720,6 @@
   'memmem',
   'mmap',
   'newlocale',
-  'pipe2',
   'poll',
   'prlimit',
   'readlink',
